The game is fun and entertaining.  However the patron status buy-in is overpriced.  Sorry, when I can get NetFlix HD for 11 bucks a month or Amazon Prime with tons of entertainment value for under 10 bucks a month that includes 2-day shipping to boot...sorry game devs/publishers- 15 bucks is way overpriced for a monthly fee.  Not sure who came up with the magic 15 dollar number but it is lame and outdated.  In comparison, my kids and I have had our 'family' account on Wizards 101 for years now, that is a fair price for good entertainment.
So take the huge handicap you get for not being a patron on top of some unnecessary mechanics (labor system) and around level 20 this game starts to get stale.  This would have definitely been a better B2P model like GW2.  Trion at one time was top of my list for games I played when Rift was released.  But now in my mind I compare it to PWI and Aeria, greedy meh company with meh games.
